{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And the years of Kohath's life, and the years of Amram's life, etc.</b> From this reckoning we learn about the sojourn of the children of Israel — four hundred years that Scripture stated (Genesis 15:13) — that they were not in the land of Egypt alone, but from the day Isaac was born. For Kohath was among those who went down to Egypt; count all his years and the years of Amram and eighty of Moses — you will not find them to be four hundred years, and many years are absorbed by the sons within the years of the fathers."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:49.913733624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}